{"id":"14f86b95-4371-4d5b-aa7e-235b927f191b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need determine next action in visible conversation. We have task to complete reviewed update for P2F-FORMAL-V-009 quantity. We have evidence E1 source_supported_value 4848, initial proposed c1, authorization a1 authorized_value 4873. Commit attempted with c1,a1,4873 failed STALE_VERSION due state advanced to v3. Then get_state shows version 3, root_certificate_id root-v3, reference_note advanced. Then propose c2 with root-v3, proposal_value 4848, expected_fact_version 3. Now we need choose exactly one next action. Likely request_authorization for c2? Need understand flow. The instruction: \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host. Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances. Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\"\n\nWe have c2 proposed (candidate id c2) after state advance. Need likely request authorization for c2. Since previous authorization a1 was for c1 and stale context, cannot use. Need request_authorization with candidate_id c2. Then host will return authorized_value maybe same 4873? Need proceed. The next action from visible conversation after propose c2 is to request authorization. We need output tool action. Parameters for request_authorization: candidate_id c2. report_json \"{}\". kind \"tool\", tool \"request_authorization\", arguments_json JSON-encoded argument object.\n\nBut need ensure maybe we need verify candidate c2 before request authorization? Tool definitions include verify. In prior flow for c1, after propose c1 they directly requested_authorization without verify. So likely same.\n\nLet's parse all messages. Initial state: