receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\"\n\nSo source-supported value is 4848. Propose that. Request host review. Host authorized value 4873. Then commit should use 4873. Commit failed stale version. After state advance, we re-propose? We did propose c2 with 4848. But maybe the correct next step is to request authorization for c2, then the host will again return authorized value? But the explicit authorized value already returned was 4873. However since candidate c1 is stale, its authorization may be stale. The instruction says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" Could we re-commit c1 with same a1 but new version? No, candidate c1 tied to root-v2 expected_fact_version 2, so commit fails STALE_VERSION. Need new candidate c2 with root-v3 expected_fact_version 3. But c2 proposal is 4848, not 4873. Is that correct? The proposal should be source-supported value 4848. The host review then may authorize 4873. So next action request_authorization c2.\n\nBut let's consider if c2 proposal_value should be 4873? The source-supported value is 4848. The host explicitly authorized 4873 (maybe an adjustment). The task says \"Propose the source-supported value and request the host review. Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So you propose source-supported 4848, then host returns authorized value 4873, then commit 4873. When re-proposing after state advance, should we propose the source-supported value again (4848) or the authorized value (4873)? The flow: propose creates candidate from evidence. The candidate is an AI suggestion. It should contain source-supported value 4848. Authorization is separate and can override to 4873. If we propose 4873, that may be treating the preview candidate as authorized, or not source-supported. So c2 with 4848 is correct. Then request_authorization for c2. The host may return authorized_value 4873 again. So next action is request_authorization c2.\n\nCould there be a need to verify c2 before requesting authorization? The previous flow didn't. But maybe after state advance, need verify? Tool verify takes candidate_id. In initial flow, after propose c1, they did request_authorization directly. So likely no.\n\nCould there be a business preview deliverable? The task mentions \"Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\" No explicit preview deliverable in conversation. So ignore.\n\nNow answer exactly one JSON object with no prose/code fences.\n\nWe need output valid JSON. Ensure arguments_json is a string, so escape inner quotes. For final if we were done, we'd have kind final etc. But next action is tool.\n\nLet's verify the keys: kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. For tool: kind \"tool\", tool \"request_authorization\", arguments_json JSON-encoded string, report_json \"{}\".\n\nSo final:\n\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"request_authorization\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nCheck if any other parameters required? request_authorization only candidate_id. Yes.\n\nThus answer.","signature":"14f86b95-4371-4d5b-aa7e-235b927f191b"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"request_authorization\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":463,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2560,"output_tokens":1584,"service_tier":"standard"}}